    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is anchored by the dual-threat upside of **Kyle Tucker** (84.92) and **Gunnar Henderson** (83.30). **Kyle Tucker** benefits from an elite matchup against Gibson, whose poor xERA (5.63) provides the highest run-scoring potential of the slate, while **Gunnar Henderson** maintains high value despite facing Sasaki; his score is buoyed by his ability to exploit the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which maximizes his stolen base potential\u2014the most critical variable for our 5x5 objectives. **Andy Pages** (72.66) also capitalizes on the same favorable Gibson matchup, slotting into the two-hole with a strong platoon projection, while **Nolan Schanuel** (67.23) and **Josh Jung** (65.53) offer the most reliable floor-to-ceiling combinations given their favorable park adjustments and high-leverage lineup spots.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (54.37) in favor of **Cole Carrigg** (64.40). While **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** possesses a solid dynamic platoon advantage, his efficiency was suppressed by a subpar park factor, whereas **Cole Carrigg** benefits from a 14% park boost and the utility of switch-hitting, providing a safer overall output. We are monitoring **Jackson Merrill** (52.34) closely; despite his elite sprint speed, his matchup against deGrom is an objective risk, as the pitcher's elite hold skills significantly dampen our SB-focused strategy. Conversely, we are keeping **Wade Meckler** (45.61) in the lineup despite his low score, as we need his presence to protect our volume in the deeper OF slots. Managers should be aware that the catcher tandem of **Drake Baldwin** (47.55) and **Liam Hicks** (52.95) remains in the marginal bucket today, specifically due to tough pitching matchups against Misiorowski and Roupp, respectively; we are strictly managing their plate appearances to preserve our annual game caps while chasing any available runs in their top-of-order spots.",
